'''Season five''' of ''[[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series)|Dancing with the Stars]]'' premiered on September 24, 2007, with a special three-night premiere week, on the [[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] network. As with previous seasons, [[CTV Television Network]] aired the series in Canada.<ref>{{cite web| url= http://www.ctv.ca/servlet/ArticleNews/show/CTVShows/20060811/Home-DancingwiththeStars/20070828/| title= CTV.ca: Dancing with the Stars| url-status= dead| archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20070919191209/http://www.ctv.ca/servlet/ArticleNews/show/CTVShows/20060811/Home-DancingwiththeStars/20070828/| archive-date= 2007-09-19}}</ref>

On November 27, 2007, [[IndyCar]] driver [[Hélio Castroneves]] and [[Julianne Hough]] were crowned the champions, while [[Spice Girls]] singer [[Mel B]] and [[Maksim Chmerkovskiy]] finished in second place, and entertainer [[Marie Osmond]] and [[Jonathan Roberts (dancer)|Jonathan Roberts]] finished third.

==Cast==
===Couples===
This season featured twelve celebrity contestants. On August 29, 2007, the cast was announced on ''[[Good Morning America]]'' by [[Tom Bergeron]], [[Carrie Ann Inaba]], and reigning celebrity champion [[Apolo Anton Ohno]].<ref>{{Cite web|url = http://www.cbsnews.com/news/dancing-with-the-stars-cast-announced/|title = "Dancing With The Stars" Cast Announced|date = August 29, 2007|access-date = May 15, 2014|work = CBS News|last = Faber|first = Judy|archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20140517120817/http://www.cbsnews.com/news/dancing-with-the-stars-cast-announced/|archive-date = May 17, 2014|url-status = live}}</ref>
